{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias across the whole 30d horizon: forecasts are systematically below realized prices (often by ~2–5 EUR, occasionally more). Apply an upward level shift to the entire path.",
    "Underestimation increases with horizon (error grows from near-0/low on days 1–3 to materially negative by ~days 7–30). Use a horizon-dependent uplift (small early, larger mid/late).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag in bullish regimes: when the recent history is turning up from a dip, the model follows too slowly and misses sustained rallies. Add momentum/acceleration term based on last 5–10 day slope and slope change.",
    "Missed volatility on upside: the model smooths peaks and fails to capture sharp upward moves (spikes/rallies). Inflate upside moves when short-term momentum is positive and realized volatility is rising.",
    "Mean-reversion assumption too strong: forecasts revert toward ~62–66 even when the market transitions to a higher regime (~67–70). Introduce regime shift detection (e.g., break above recent 20–30d range) and lift the forecast baseline accordingly."
  ]
}
